@@ -8,6 +8,17 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute()` now validates incoming tool arguments against each tool's declared JSON Schema
+  `inputSchema` before calling the executor. Invalid arguments return a `ToolResponse` naming the failing
+  property paths and constraints — never echoing or logging input values — so the orchestrator feeds the
+  rejection back to the model as a `tool_result` within the tool-round budget rather than failing the stream.
+  Static tool schemas are compiled once at `register()` time and throw naming the tool if invalid; extra
+  undeclared properties still pass through unchanged without type coercion or injected defaults. Executors
+  that previously saw malformed inputs to return custom errors will now only receive inputs that satisfy
+  their `inputSchema`.
+
